{:edb/committed true :edb/basis-t 451 :edb/replayed false :edb/tx-hash "505fb064d2f4f958ea7096c01c9a80798dcb94df2872a5e006fa572b9ad67fdf" :edb/db-before-t 450 :edb/db-after-t 451 :edb/tx-data [[13194139533763 50 #inst "2026-10-04T20:49:54.660Z" 13194139533763 true] [17592186054583 1020 #edb/ref 17592186249835 13194139533763 true] [17592186060189 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139533763 true] [17592186060189 1145 "First, we find an angle that's coterminal with $-{450}^{∘}$ by *adding* integer multiples of ${360}^{∘}$ until we get an angle that lies in the range $[{0}^{∘},{360}^{∘}).$\n\n- $-{450}^{∘}+{360}^{∘}=-90$\n\n- $-{450}^{∘}+2\\cdot {360}^{∘}={270}^{∘}\\,✓$\n\nSo the angle ${270}^{∘}$ is coterminal with $-{450}^{∘}.$ Let's draw this coterminal angle in the coordinate plane.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13939908/assets/35b9783c9ac87b0a8d177e7bdf340b48513146404b7c768a8532da59b6ec7948.png)\n\nWe see that ${270}^{∘}$ lies between quadrants III and IV. Therefore, $-{450}^{∘}$ also lies between these quadrants." 13194139533763 true] [17592186069200 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139533763 true] [17592186069200 1145 "To compute\n\n$$\n\\frac{2a{b}^{2}}{b{c}^{3}}÷\\frac{8{a}^{3}}{7{c}^{4}},\n$$\n\nwe just need to multiply by the reciprocal of the divisor:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2a{b}^{2}}{b{c}^{3}}÷\\frac{8{a}^{3}}{7{c}^{4}} & = \\\\ \\frac{2a{b}^{2}}{b{c}^{3}}\\cdot \\frac{7{c}^{4}}{8{a}^{3}} & = \\\\ \\frac{2ab\\cdot b}{b{c}^{3}}\\cdot \\frac{7c\\cdot {c}^{3}}{4\\cdot 2a\\cdot {a}^{2}} & = \\\\ \\frac{\\cancel{2a}b\\cdot \\cancel{b}}{\\cancel{b}\\cancel{{c}^{3}}}\\cdot \\frac{7c\\cdot \\cancel{{c}^{3}}}{4\\cdot \\cancel{2a}\\cdot {a}^{2}} & = \\\\ \\frac{7bc}{4{a}^{2}} & \\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533763 true] [17592186073755 1020 #edb/ref 17592186249828 13194139533763 true] [17592186083300 1020 #edb/ref 17592186249841 13194139533763 true] [17592186083449 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139533763 true] [17592186083449 1145 "Given a polynomial with integer coefficients, the rational roots theorem states that any rational roots of the polynomial must take the form\n\n$$\n\\pm \\frac{\\text{factor of the constant term}}{\\text{factor of the leading coefficient}}.\n$$\n\nFor the given polynomial:\n\n- The constant term is $-2,$ and its factors are $\\pm 1$ and $\\pm 2.$\n\n- The leading coefficient is $2,$ and its factors are $\\pm 1$ and $\\pm 2.$\n\nFirst, we list out all the possibilities for the numerator and denominator:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\pm \\frac{1}{1}, & \\pm \\frac{1}{2}, \\\\ \\pm \\frac{2}{1}, & \\pm \\frac{2}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we reduce the fractions to lowest terms:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\pm 1, & \\pm \\frac{1}{2}, \\\\ \\pm 2, & \\pm 1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNotice that some potential roots are duplicates (shown above in red). Removing these duplicates, and listing those remaining in order from least to greatest in absolute value, we have\n\n$$\n\\pm \\frac{1}{2},\\,\\pm 1,\\,\\pm 2.\n$$\n\nThis makes a total of $6$ potential roots. (Remember that each $\\pm $ sign accounts for $2$ roots, and $2\\cdot 3=6.$)" 13194139533763 true] [17592186087695 1020 #edb/ref 17592186249848 13194139533763 true] [17592186192641 1020 #edb/ref 17592186249838 13194139533763 true] [17592186249828 1017 #edb/ref 17592186249829 13194139533763 true] [17592186249828 1089 "q-118944" 13194139533763 true] [17592186249828 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139533763 true] [17592186249828 1100 "Consider the points $A(-3s,-4s,7s)$ and $B(s,-6s,3s).$ Given that the distance between $A$ and $B$ is $54,$ find the possible values of $s.$" 13194139533763 true] [17592186249828 1113 #uuid "3329b56b-ec4b-5fc6-8723-d1077c57a901" 13194139533763 true] [17592186249828 1145 "The distance $d$ between two points $A({x}_{1},{y}_{1},{z}_{1})$ and $B({x}_{2},{y}_{2},{z}_{2})$ is given by\n\n$$\nd=\\sqrt{({x}_{2}-{x}_{1})^{2}+({y}_{2}-{y}_{1})^{2}+({z}_{2}-{z}_{1})^{2}}.\n$$\n\nIn this case, we have $A{{(-3s,-4s,7s)}_{⏟}}_{\\text{(}{x}_{1}\\text{, }{y}_{1}\\text{, }{z}_{1}\\text{)}}$ and $B{{(s,-6s,3s)}_{⏟}}_{\\text{(}{x}_{2}\\text{, }{y}_{2}\\text{, }{z}_{2}\\text{)}}.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}d & =\\sqrt{(s-(-3s))^{2}+(-6s-(-4s))^{2}+(3s-7s)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(4s)^{2}+(-2s)^{2}+(-4s)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{16{s}^{2}+4{s}^{2}+16{s}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{36{s}^{2}} \\\\  & =6\\,|s|.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, since $d=54,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}6\\,|s| & =54 \\\\ |s| & =9 \\\\ s & =\\pm 9.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533763 true] [17592186249829 1000 #edb/ref 17592186249830 13194139533763 true] [17592186249829 1000 #edb/ref 17592186249831 13194139533763 true] [17592186249829 1000 #edb/ref 17592186249832 13194139533763 true] [17592186249829 1000 #edb/ref 17592186249833 13194139533763 true] [17592186249829 1000 #edb/ref 17592186249834 13194139533763 true] [17592186249829 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139533763 true] [17592186249829 1041 "selection" 13194139533763 true] [17592186249829 1104 #edb/ref 17592186249834 13194139533763 true] [17592186249829 1110 #uuid "c2a37dcf-9eee-593f-b167-d4ee34dd3a0a" 13194139533763 true] [17592186249830 1034 "9" 13194139533763 true] [17592186249830 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533763 true] [17592186249830 1111 #uuid "e40a6195-e0a6-5569-962b-194638c1b2ed" 13194139533763 true] [17592186249831 1034 "6" 13194139533763 true] [17592186249831 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533763 true] [17592186249831 1111 #uuid "6789bb35-fc2a-529d-89ea-8706539aeccc" 13194139533763 true] [17592186249832 1034 "\\pm 6" 13194139533763 true] [17592186249832 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533763 true] [17592186249832 1111 #uuid "0e71e43a-0165-58ba-861e-1e7ac75f1539" 13194139533763 true] [17592186249833 1034 "\\pm 3" 13194139533763 true] [17592186249833 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533763 true] [17592186249833 1111 #uuid "64137b70-d0e1-5f89-afa3-14159ebf7acc" 13194139533763 true] [17592186249834 1034 "\\pm 9" 13194139533763 true] [17592186249834 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533763 true] [17592186249834 1111 #uuid "6b70beb1-4d50-5923-a65b-f63e167fe831" 13194139533763 true] [17592186249835 1017 #edb/ref 17592186249836 13194139533763 true] [17592186249835 1089 "q-237438" 13194139533763 true] [17592186249835 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139533763 true] [17592186249835 1100 "If ${a}_{n+2}={a}_{n+1}+{a}_{n}$ with ${a}_{1}=0$ and ${a}_{2}=3,$ then ${a}_{3}=${{field-1}}." 13194139533763 true] [17592186249835 1113 #uuid "9fb3c079-a60e-5bda-bfec-324752a909a3" 13194139533763 true] [17592186249835 1145 "The recursive formula is\n\n$$\n{a}_{n+2}={a}_{n+1}+{a}_{n}.\n$$\n\nSubstituting $n=1$ into the recursive formula gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{1+2} & ={a}_{1+1}+{a}_{1} \\\\ {a}_{3} & ={a}_{2}+{a}_{1} \\\\ {a}_{3} & =3+0 \\\\ {a}_{3} & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533763 true] [17592186249836 1000 #edb/ref 17592186249837 13194139533763 true] [17592186249836 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139533763 true] [17592186249836 1041 "field-1" 13194139533763 true] [17592186249836 1104 #edb/ref 17592186249837 13194139533763 true] [17592186249836 1110 #uuid "f80d8a3c-fc64-51cd-b4fe-2ae93b210522" 13194139533763 true] [17592186249837 1034 "3" 13194139533763 true] [17592186249837 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533763 true] [17592186249837 1111 #uuid "db112308-76e2-59ee-a782-d3af4c5c73c5" 13194139533763 true] [17592186249838 1017 #edb/ref 17592186249839 13194139533763 true] [17592186249838 1089 "q-276793" 13194139533763 true] [17592186249838 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139533763 true] [17592186249838 1100 "The function $f(x)=\\frac{5}{kx-1}$ has an inverse function given by ${f}^{-1}(x)=\\frac{5+x}{x}.$ What is the value of $k?$\n\n$k=$\n{{field-1}}" 13194139533763 true] [17592186249838 1113 #uuid "fb65edc8-082c-52ff-844e-1ac02a93d381" 13194139533763 true] [17592186249838 1145 "To find ${f}^{-1}(x),$ we start by replacing $f(x)$ with $y:$\n\n$$\ny=\\frac{5}{kx-1}\n$$\n\nNow, interchanging $x$ and $y$ gives\n\n$$\nx=\\frac{5}{ky-1}.\n$$\n\nThen, we make $y$ the subject of the equation, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =\\frac{5}{ky-1} \\\\ x(ky-1) & =5 \\\\ kxy-x & =5 \\\\ kxy & =5+x \\\\ y & =\\frac{5+x}{kx}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the inverse function is \n\n$$\n{f}^{-1}(x)=\\frac{5+x}{kx}.\n$$\n\nComparing our answer with the given expression, we conclude that $k=1.$" 13194139533763 true] [17592186249839 1000 #edb/ref 17592186249840 13194139533763 true] [17592186249839 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139533763 true] [17592186249839 1041 "field-1" 13194139533763 true] [17592186249839 1104 #edb/ref 17592186249840 13194139533763 true] [17592186249839 1110 #uuid "548003a4-06f8-530b-a264-d0ff9736ac62" 13194139533763 true] [17592186249840 1034 "1" 13194139533763 true] [17592186249840 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533763 true] [17592186249840 1111 #uuid "c95ceacd-c9bc-5cec-b342-df5855bba0cd" 13194139533763 true] [17592186249841 1017 #edb/ref 17592186249842 13194139533763 true] [17592186249841 1089 "q-288779" 13194139533763 true] [17592186249841 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139533763 true] [17592186249841 1100 "Consider the quadratic equation\n\n$$\n3{x}^{2}+8x-1=0.\n$$\n\n**Without** solving the equation, determine the sum of its solutions." 13194139533763 true] [17592186249841 1113 #uuid "70cecb06-4a85-561a-ae02-e92e4d923c8d" 13194139533763 true] [17592186249841 1145 "Suppose the quadratic equation\n\n$$\na{x}^{2}+bx+c=0\n$$\n\nhas the solutions $x={x}_{1}$ and $x={x}_{2},$ where $a\\ne 0.$ \n\nThen, Vieta's formulas state the following:\n\n- The sum of the solutions is given by\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}=-\\frac{b}{a}.\n$$\n\n- The product of the solutions is given by\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}\\cdot {x}_{2}=\\frac{c}{a}.\n$$\n\nFor the given quadratic equation, we have\n\n$$\na=3,\\,b=8,\\,c=-1.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the sum of the solutions is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{b}{a} & =-\\frac{8}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533763 true] [17592186249842 1000 #edb/ref 17592186249843 13194139533763 true] [17592186249842 1000 #edb/ref 17592186249844 13194139533763 true] [17592186249842 1000 #edb/ref 17592186249845 13194139533763 true] [17592186249842 1000 #edb/ref 17592186249846 13194139533763 true] [17592186249842 1000 #edb/ref 17592186249847 13194139533763 true] [17592186249842 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139533763 true] [17592186249842 1041 "selection" 13194139533763 true] [17592186249842 1104 #edb/ref 17592186249845 13194139533763 true] [17592186249842 1110 #uuid "11504366-ff1e-5f73-a407-cb0484718acb" 13194139533763 true] [17592186249843 1034 "-\\frac{5}{3}" 13194139533763 true] [17592186249843 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533763 true] [17592186249843 1111 #uuid "74be56fe-6024-5e32-bb17-f6bb442cdfa9" 13194139533763 true] [17592186249844 1034 "\\frac{8}{3}" 13194139533763 true] [17592186249844 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533763 true] [17592186249844 1111 #uuid "15a875f2-d2d5-5c06-9198-8435fb0d4aff" 13194139533763 true] [17592186249845 1034 "-\\frac{8}{3}" 13194139533763 true] [17592186249845 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533763 true] [17592186249845 1111 #uuid "2e6ca8d9-e8dd-57be-846f-25ff22488b22" 13194139533763 true] [17592186249846 1034 "-\\frac{7}{3}" 13194139533763 true] [17592186249846 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533763 true] [17592186249846 1111 #uuid "12fa5be9-1ba2-562a-b62c-04e01dad2d90" 13194139533763 true] [17592186249847 1034 "\\frac{7}{3}" 13194139533763 true] [17592186249847 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533763 true] [17592186249847 1111 #uuid "84d1f0c9-4e7e-5f5c-90bd-dbf09292e16a" 13194139533763 true] [17592186249848 1017 #edb/ref 17592186249849 13194139533763 true] [17592186249848 1089 "q-319492" 13194139533763 true] [17592186249848 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139533763 true] [17592186249848 1100 "Find, **in radians**, the argument of $z=-5+3\\text{i}.$ Round your final answer to **two decimal places**.\n\n**Hint**: The argument of a complex number is in the range $[0,2\\pi ).$\n\n$\\operatorname{arg}⁡(z)≈$\n{{field-1}}" 13194139533763 true] [17592186249848 1113 #uuid "18ca621b-aa9c-527c-a411-a69f8c48899c" 13194139533763 true] [17592186249848 1142 true 13194139533763 true] [17592186249848 1145 "Let's plot $z$ in the complex plane.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13939908/assets/217fc7ba4c6a6c18d0be184a9d5cc7b0a682ed2bd0da6e284955040643bc2e03.png)\n\nThe complex number $z$ lies in the second quadrant of the complex plane. Hence $\\frac{\\pi }{2}<\\operatorname{arg}⁡(z)<\\pi .$\n\nIf $\\alpha $ is the angle that $z$ makes with the negative real axis, then\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{tan}⁡\\alpha  & =\\frac{3}{5} \\\\ \\alpha  & =arctan\\,(\\frac{3}{5}) \\\\  & =0.540\\,419…\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\theta =\\operatorname{arg}⁡(z)=\\pi -0.540\\,419…≈2.60,\n$$\n\nrounded to $2$ decimal places." 13194139533763 true] [17592186249849 1000 #edb/ref 17592186249850 13194139533763 true] [17592186249849 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139533763 true] [17592186249849 1041 "field-1" 13194139533763 true] [17592186249849 1104 #edb/ref 17592186249850 13194139533763 true] [17592186249849 1110 #uuid "7ac20aed-4025-5c62-9c23-22fcb072ca0f" 13194139533763 true] [17592186249850 1034 "2.60" 13194139533763 true] [17592186249850 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533763 true] [17592186249850 1111 #uuid "cdcf49bb-f7e2-5c23-9333-af5c047c56cd" 13194139533763 true]] :edb/tempids {"q-118944" 17592186249828 "q-118944/selection" 17592186249829 "q-118944/selection/303632d9519e4b7e53f9af56aad03bb866b8b5ede58a0b8b2cb848d575460c53" 17592186249830 "q-118944/selection/a0e0e68f25b8b46aafef3b74aff7beff7fddc6de5bf36921680b04c7b0e6ffaa" 17592186249831 "q-118944/selection/add48b243ebaf46eba7641661c03d006608a5acdecbbc38b771c9f737352650c" 17592186249832 "q-118944/selection/e9b0fcc914cbb593541eab0f5a07d912a354e5fbae56d539c8